From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:14:45 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] gpiomem: pad to the CPU's maximum clock, refuse outputs
 at the start, fail loud

Re-review 3 of the /dev/gpiomem backend.

The rate. The pad is calibrated once, in take_bus(), before Ice40 times the
image (so calibration is no longer in the chunk time check_rate measures),
at the clock cpufreq reports (scaling_cur_freq, cpuinfo_min_freq,
cpuinfo_max_freq; a calibration run that straddles a clock change is
discarded) and scaled to the maximum clock, taking every cost as CPU-bound.
The same numbers scaled to the minimum clock must still give a bit of 1 us or
less, or the load stops: 1 MHz stays reachable. cpufreq unreadable, out of
order, or never still: the load stops, nothing is guessed. The timer, the
spin and cpufreq go through Ice40GpioRegs so a test can keep a virtual
clock. The claim "whatever the CPU runs at" is gone; the header says what the
pad rests on (posted writes reach the pins no sooner than they are issued)
and that the hardware trial measures the real rate. The pad is just
25 ns - w: the period term was dead (3w + 2 pad = 50 ns + w follows).

The start state. A line that is an output at the start (CDONE included) is
refused with the pins named and the commands that put them back
(pinctrl set <n> ip); alternate functions are still refused. CRESET_B is let
go by restore_functions() only if every bus line before it read back as
saved (the old code let it go regardless).

Exits and races. The GPFSEL read-modify-write and restore_functions() block
the handled signals (sigprocmask), so a handler cannot land between the read
and the write. The header names what the kernel no longer does here: the
other writer to a pin of the same GPFSEL register, the exits that leave pins
driven (SIGKILL, SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGABRT, abort, std::terminate, exit,
_exit), and the handled signals.

Selection. A compatible that does not exist is not a device-tree host
(libgpiod); one that exists and cannot be read stops the load.

Also: the GPSETn citation is section 6.1 (6.2 is the alternate function
table); "at or under 20 MHz"; "with margin" dropped.

